ComfyUI-SolAttn-H3
Copyright 2026

This project is an integration of Sol-Attn with ComfyUI. The kernel itself is
not vendored here — it is installed as the `sol-attn` package from NVlabs.

===============================================================================
Sol-Attn / Sol-Engine
===============================================================================

The `sol-attn` kernel (0.5.0) and the reference MiniMax-H3 integration this node
is modelled on both come from:

    NVlabs/Sana, sol-engine branch
    https://github.com/NVlabs/Sana/tree/sol-engine
    License: Apache License 2.0

Specifically:

  * techniques/sparse_backends/            -> the `sol-attn` package, installed
  * models/minimax_h3/optimized/sol_attn_h3.py
        -> source of the policy: tau=1.0, sink over the prefix, first N steps
           and first 2 layers dense, correctness gate at tau=-1000, routing
           density probe

Publication:

    Sol-Attn: Accelerating Video Generation Inference via On-the-Fly
    Attention Sparsification
    Li, Haopeng; Li, Yitong; Chen, Junsong; Ye, Tian; Liu, Haozhe; Yu, Jincheng;
    Wang, Duomin; Zhang, Ruihua; Xie, Zeke; Xie, Enze; Han, Song
    arXiv:2607.24027 (2026)

===============================================================================
Divergences from the reference
===============================================================================

Three design decisions differ from `sol_attn_h3.py`, each because ComfyUI
exposes information the SGLang runtime did not:

  1. The step index is read from `transformer_options["sample_sigmas"]` rather
     than guessed from the direction of timestep change.
  2. The sink range comes from `PackedLayout.segments` rather than being
     inferred from discontinuities in `video_indices`.
  3. The gate criterion for the worst element is relative (`max_rel`) rather
     than absolute (`max_abs`); `mean_abs` and `rel_l2` are unchanged. The
     measurement behind that decision is in the README and in the `run_gate`
     docstring.
